Only Rodney and those named demons who are summoners are capable of
summoning non-unique cursers outside of Hell, however.  Outside of Hell,
all calls to summon nasties result in the appearance of a mob of
nasties. The list of nasties contains exactly one spellcasting monster,
the arch-lich.  The nasties selector will never pick a wizardly
spellcaster with a MONSTR greater than or equal to the caster's MONSTR.
Everything with a MONSTR greater than an arch-lich is unique.

In Hell, any casting of summon nasties has a 10% chance of becoming an
attempt to summon a demon.  This has a 5% chance of yielding a demon
prince, a 23.75% chance of yielding a demon lord, a 53.4375% chance of
yielding one non-unique demon, and a 17.8125% chance of yielding two
non-unique demons.  If all princes are dead, further attempts to summon
a prince will summon a lord; if all lords are dead, further attempts to
summon a lord will summon a non-unique demon.

The following '&' can curse items: nalfeshnee, Orcus, Dispater, and
Demogorgon.

So, in practice, you are relatively unlikely to have a summoner summon
a curse-capable monster unless the summoning summoner is the Wizard of
Yendor, Orcus, Dispater, or Demogorgon.
